We then work our way backwards from the end of the string to find the three extensions. Once we have the location of the third extension, we use `sprintf` to modify the filename as per requirement and make it null terminated at that point. If there are less than three extensions in the filename or if they are not consecutive, then only the last one is processed and rest are made null-terminated.
