        if (pthread_create(&threads[i], NULL, (void *(*)(void *))logAndValidate, pdu) != 0) {
            fprintf(stderr, "Failed to create thread\n");
            free(pdu);
            return i;  // Return the number of PDUs successfully created.
        }

        list[i] = pdu;  // Add each validated and logged PDU to the list.
    }

    for (int j=0; j<M; j++) {
        if(pthread_join(threads[j], NULL) != 0){
            fprintf(stderr, "Error joining thread\n");
            return i;  // Return the number of PDUs successfully created.
        }
    }

    return M;  // All PDUs were successfully created and processed.
}
```
This is a basic implementation of your request using C. The actual code may vary depending on the specific requirements of your project such as your predefined thresholds for `CRCFLAG`, how to initialize `RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG` and generate random numbers etc. 
Also, be aware that it's not possible to ensure thread safety when accessed concurrently from multiple threads in C because of the Global Interpreter Lock (GIL) which prevents truly parallel native threading in Python. For multithreading in C, you can use POSIX Threads (pthreads), OpenMP or C++11 threads.
']

